Specifications Driven Development
3 minutes

"This slide summarizes the biggest lesson I took away from the project.

AI is very good at generating things.

What's becoming more important is everything that happens before and after generation."

Point to Design Specification.

"Before asking AI to build something, we need a clear design.

What problem are we solving?
What assumptions are we making?
What are the failure scenarios?

The quality of the specification often determines the quality of the output."

Move to Code Review.

"The second lesson is around review.

One thing I noticed repeatedly is that AI gives very confident answers.

Sometimes those answers are correct.
Sometimes they are not.

So I found myself spending less time writing code and more time reviewing assumptions, edge cases, and hidden gaps."


Move to Production Readiness.

"The third lesson is production readiness.

Just because AI can generate working code doesn't mean the system is production ready.

We still need validation, resiliency, rollback plans, observability, security, and operational controls."

Then finish with the bottom observations.

"So my biggest takeaway is this:

AI reduced the effort required to generate code.

But it increased the importance of design, review, and engineering judgment.

The review process became just as important as the generation process.

And while AI can help us move faster, humans still need to remain accountable for the decisions that ultimately reach production."

